<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 6-mth T-bill avg yield falls to 14.52 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 6-mth T-bill avg yield falls to 14.52 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 14.52 percent annual at an auction on June 9 from 16.24 percent at the last auction on May 27, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   June 9	     May 27</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ46K1112973     KZ46K2711971</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  750</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 2,400		2,830</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 600		  792</p>
<p> Average price			 93.23 pct	  92.49</p>
<p> Average yield			 14.52 pct	  16.24</p>
<p> Tenor				   182 days	   182 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Dec 11, 1997     Nov 27, 1997</p>
<p>$1=75.60 tenge</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
